From c49e5d074ae78bddf6fabdcb10c9945a95c2d5c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:18:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(remote): accumulate streamed tool calls by index

OpenAI-compatible servers stream parallel tool calls interleaved and keyed by
`index` (index 0 frag, index 1 frag, index 0 frag, ...). processToolCallChunk
started a new call only when an `id` arrived and appended every other argument
fragment to the last call, so models that emit several calls at once (GLM,
Kimi K2) got two calls' JSON concatenated into one and the turn failed on
JSON.parse ("Unexpected end of JSON input").

Accumulate per index. A different id at an index that already has a call still
starts a new call (servers that reuse index 0 with a fresh id per call), and
fragments without an index keep the old id / last-call behaviour.

Ported from fl4p/off-grid-ai-mobile a781199d8 (Fabian), adjusted for the
index-0-reuse case.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
